{"id":"8eafe049f935b1488ce285b9b315224cb0256fc7","axis":"silent","repo":"nrwl/nx","sha":"8eafe049f935b1488ce285b9b315224cb0256fc7","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/guides/Nx","lines":["@@ -108,3 +108,30 @@ Enable `applyPreidToDependents` when:"," Leave it off (the default) when a stable `1.0.1` of `project-a` depending on an `rc` of `project-b` is a valid, intentional release for you. Prerelease dependencies shouldn't automatically promote their consumers into prereleases."," "," The option can also be set per release group under `release.groups.<group>.version.applyPreidToDependents` to scope the behavior to only certain groups.","+","+### Check the release boundary","+","+When you release a subset of your workspace with `--groups` or `--projects`, dependency relationships can cross the edge of that subset.","+Set `version.releaseBoundaryCheck` to `\"warn\"` or `\"error\"` to have Nx report them after it determines the new versions and before it writes them:","+","+```json","+{","+  \"release\": {","+    \"version\": {","+      \"releaseBoundaryCheck\": \"error\"","+    }","+  }","+}","+```","+","+The check reports three types of finding, named by their `type` in the programmatic API result:","+","+- `added-by-dependents`: a project you didn't select is being released because `updateDependents` added it. With the default of `\"always\"`, releasing `group-a` also releases any project in `group-b` that depends on a released project.","+- `dependent-not-released`: a project depends on a released project but isn't released itself. Nx shows the version it declares and, for `package.json` projects where both are valid semver, whether that declared version admits the new version. If it does, consumers of the dependent can resolve the new version without the dependent being released or tested again.","+- `dependency-not-released`: a released project depends on a project that isn't being released but has pending changes. Nx estimates the pending bump with the conventional commits or version plans of that project's release group. When it can't, for example because the group uses the interactive prompt or has no matching git tag, it reports the pending changes as unknown.","+","+With `\"error\"`, any finding fails the release, so a release that `updateDependents: \"always\"` extends into another group fails too.","+To release one group at a time without `added-by-dependents` findings, set `updateDependents` to `\"auto\"` or `\"never\"`.","+Dependents in other groups are then reported as `dependent-not-released` instead.","+","+The check only covers projects that are in a release group, and it doesn't cover Docker versioning."],"additions":27,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/reference/nx-json.mdoc","lines":["@@ -756,6 +756,33 @@ When versioning with `--preid`, the implicit patch bumps given to dependents (an"," "," Set `version.applyPreidToDependents` to `true` if you want the `--preid` value to flow through to those side-effectful bumps instead. It can also be set per release group under `release.groups.<group>.version.applyPreidToDependents`. See [Update Dependents](/docs/guides/nx-release/update-dependents#propagating---preid-to-dependent-bumps) for the full walkthrough and guidance on when to enable it."," ","+#### Release boundary check","+","+`version.releaseBoundaryCheck` checks a release for dependency relationships that cross the boundary of what's being released.","+It runs after Nx determines the new versions and before Nx writes them, which is after any pre-version commands have run.","+The values are `\"off\"` (the default), `\"warn\"`, and `\"error\"`.","+It's only supported at the root level, not per release group.","+","+```jsonc","+// nx.json","+{","+  \"release\": {","+    \"version\": {","+      \"releaseBoundaryCheck\": \"warn\",","+    },","+  },","+}","+```","+","+With `\"warn\"`, Nx prints the findings and continues.","+With `\"error\"`, Nx prints the findings and fails before writing the new versions.","+The `releaseVersion` and `release` programmatic APIs return the findings as `releaseBoundaryFindings`, or reject with a `ReleaseBoundaryCheckError` whose `findings` property holds them in `\"error\"` mode.","+Each finding has one of these `type` values:","+","+- `added-by-dependents`: a project outside the `--groups` or `--projects` selection is released because `updateDependents` added it.","+- `dependent-not-released`: a project in a release group depends on a released project but isn't released itself.","+- `dependency-not-released`: a released project depends on a project in a release group that isn't released but has pending changes, or whose pending changes Nx can't determine.","+"," ### Changelog"," "," The `changelog` property configures the changelog phase of the release process. It is used to generate a changelog for your projects, and commit it to your repository."],"additions":27,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"e2e/release/src/release-boundary-check.test.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@","+import { appendFileSync } from 'fs';","+import {","+  cleanupProject,","+  newProject,","+  readJson,","+  runCLI,","+  runCommandAsync,","+  tmpProjPath,","+  uniq,","+  updateJson,","+} from '@nx/e2e-utils';","+","+describe('nx release releaseBoundaryCheck', () => {","+  let pkgA: string;","+  let pkgB: string;","+  let pkgC: string;","+","+  const commitChange = async (pkg: string, message: string) => {","+    appendFileSync(tmpProjPath(`${pkg}/index.js`), `\\n// ${message}\\n`);","+    await runCommandAsync(`git add ${pkg}`);","+    await runCommandAsync(`git commit -m \"${message}\"`);","+  };","+","+  const setReleaseConfig = async (","+    groups: Record<string, string[]>,","+    version: Record<string, unknown>","+  ) => {","+    updateJson('nx.json', (nxJson) => {","+      nxJson.release = {","+        groups: Object.fromEntries(","+          Object.entries(groups).map(([name, projects]) => [","+            name,","+            { projectsRelationship: 'independent', projects },","+          ])","+        ),","+        version: { conventionalCommits: true, ...version },","+        changelog: { workspaceChangelog: false },","+        git: { commit: false, tag: false },","+      };","+      return nxJson;","+    });","+    await runCommandAsync(`git add nx.json`);","+    await runCommandAsync(`git commit -m \"chore: update release config\"`);","+  };","+","+  beforeAll(async () => {","+    newProject({ packages: ['@nx/js'] });","+","+    pkgA = uniq('pkg-a');","+    pkgB = uniq('pkg-b');","+    pkgC = uniq('pkg-c');","+    for (const pkg of [pkgA, pkgB, pkgC]) {","+      runCLI(`generate @nx/workspace:npm-package ${pkg}`);","+      updateJson(`${pkg}/package.json`, (json) => {","+        json.version = '1.0.0';","+        return json;","+      });","+    }","+    for (const dependent of [pkgA, pkgB]) {","+      updateJson(`${dependent}/package.json`, (json) => {","+        json.dependencies = { [`@proj/${pkgC}`]: '^1.0.0' };","+        return json;","+      });","+    }","+","+    await runCommandAsync(`git add .`);","+    await runCommandAsync(`git commit -m \"chore: initial commit\"`);","+    for (const pkg of [pkgA, pkgB, pkgC]) {","+      await runCommandAsync(`git tag ${pkg}@1.0.0`);","+    }","+    await commitChange(pkgC, `feat(${pkgC}): change c`);","+  }, 120000);","+","+  afterAll(() => cleanupProject());","+","+  it('should fail before writing anything when updateDependents adds a project from another group and the check is \"error\"', async () => {","+    await setReleaseConfig(","+      { 'group-a': [pkgA, pkgC], 'group-b': [pkgB] },","+      { releaseBoundaryCheck: 'error' }","+    );","+","+    const output = runCLI(`release --groups=group-a --skip-publish`, {","+      silenceError: true,","+    });","+","+    expect(output).toContain('The release boundary check found');","+    expect(output).toContain(","+      `\"${pkgB}\" (release group \"group-b\") was not selected, but is being released as 1.0.1 because it depends on \"${pkgC}\"`","+    );","+    expect(readJson(`${pkgC}/package.json`).version).toEqual('1.0.0');","+    expect(readJson(`${pkgB}/package.json`).version).toEqual('1.0.0');","+  }, 120000);","+","+  it('should warn about a dependent in another group that is not released and still release when the check is \"warn\"', async () => {","+    await setReleaseConfig(","+      { 'group-a': [pkgA, pkgC], 'group-b': [pkgB] },","+      { releaseBoundaryCheck: 'warn', updateDependents: 'auto' }","+    );","+","+    const output = runCLI(`release --groups=group-a --skip-publish --dry-run`, {","+      redirectStderr: true,","+    });","+","+    expect(output).toContain(","+      `\"${pkgB}\" (release group \"group-b\") is not being released, but depends on \"${pkgC}\", which is being released as 1.1.0. It declares \"^1.0.0\" in dependencies, which admits the new version without \"${pkgB}\" being released again.`","+    );","+    expect(output).toContain('New version 1.1.0 written to manifest');","+  }, 120000);","+","+  it('should warn about a dependency in another group with pending changes', async () => {","+    await setReleaseConfig(","+      { 'group-a': [pkgA], 'group-b': [pkgB], 'group-c': [pkgC] },","+      { releaseBoundaryCheck: 'warn' }","+    );","+    await commitChange(pkgA, `fix(${pkgA}): change a`);","+","+    const output = runCLI(`release --groups=group-a --skip-publish`, {","+      redirectStderr: true,","+    });","+","+    expect(output).toContain(","+      `\"${pkgA}\" is being released and depends on \"${pkgC}\" (release group \"group-c\"), which is not being released but has pending changes (a \"minor\" bump).`","+    );","+    expect(readJson(`${pkgA}/package.json`).version).toEqual('1.0.1');","+    expect(readJson(`${pkgC}/package.json`).version).toEqual('1.0.0');","+  }, 120000);","+});"],"additions":127,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/release/index.ts","lines":["@@ -11,3 +11,4 @@ export {","   AfterAllProjectsVersioned,","   ResolveVersionForDependency,"," } from '../src/command-line/release';","+export type { ReleaseBoundaryFinding } from '../src/command-line/release';"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/schemas/nx-schema.json","lines":["@@ -1375,6 +1375,12 @@","           \"type\": \"string\",","           \"description\": \"A command to run after validation of nx release configuration, but before versioning begins. Useful for preparing build artifacts. If --dry-run is passed, the command is still executed, but with the NX_DRY_RUN environment variable set to 'true'.\"","         },","+        \"releaseBoundaryCheck\": {","+          \"type\": \"string\",","+          \"enum\": [\"off\", \"warn\", \"error\"],","+          \"default\": \"off\",","+          \"description\": \"Whether to check, after the new versions are determined and before they are written, for dependency relationships that cross the boundary of what is being released: projects added to the release because they depend on something being released, dependents that are not being released, and dependencies with pending changes that are not being released. 'off' skips the check, 'warn' prints any findings and continues, and 'error' prints any findings and fails before the new versions are written.\"","+        },","         \"specifierSource\": {","           \"type\": \"string\",","           \"enum\": [\"prompt\", \"conventional-commits\", \"version-plans\"],"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/command-line/release/config/config.ts","lines":["@@ -606,10 +606,12 @@ export async function createNxReleaseConfig(","   } as DeepRequired<{","     git?: NxReleaseGitConfiguration;","     preVersionCommand?: string;","+    releaseBoundaryCheck?: 'off' | 'warn' | 'error';","   }> &","     NxReleaseVersionConfiguration;","   delete rootVersionWithoutGlobalOptions.git;","   delete rootVersionWithoutGlobalOptions.preVersionCommand;","+  delete rootVersionWithoutGlobalOptions.releaseBoundaryCheck;"," ","   // Apply conventionalCommits shorthand to the final group defaults if explicitly configured in the original user config","   if (userConfig.version?.conventionalCommits === true) {"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/command-line/release/index.ts","lines":["@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@ export const releaseChangelog = defaultClient.releaseChangelog.bind(","   defaultClient"," ) as typeof defaultClient.releaseChangelog;"," ","+/**","+ * @public","+ */","+export type { ReleaseBoundaryFinding } from './version/release-boundary-check';","+"," /**","  * @public","  */"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/command-line/release/release.ts","lines":["@@ -133,6 +133,7 @@ export function createAPI(","       workspaceVersion,","       projectsVersionData,","       releaseGraph,","+      releaseBoundaryFindings,","     }: NxReleaseVersionResult = await releaseVersion({","       ...args,","       stageChanges: shouldStage,","@@ -441,6 +442,7 @@ export function createAPI(","       workspaceVersion,","       projectsVersionData,","       releaseGraph,","+      ...(releaseBoundaryFindings && { releaseBoundaryFindings }),","     };","   };"," }"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/command-line/release/utils/release-graph.ts","lines":["@@ -699,21 +699,11 @@ export class ReleaseGraph {","     const releaseTagPattern = releaseGroup.releaseTag.pattern;"," ","     if (finalConfigForProject.currentVersionResolver === 'git-tag') {","-      latestMatchingGitTag = await getLatestGitTagForPattern(","-        releaseTagPattern,","-        {","-          projectName: sanitizeProjectNameForGitTag(projectGraphNode.name),","-          releaseGroupName: releaseGroup.name,","-        },","-        this.resolveRepositoryTags.bind(this),","-        {","-          checkAllBranchesWhen: releaseGroup.releaseTag.checkAllBranchesWhen,","-          preid: preid,","-          requireSemver: releaseGroup.releaseTag.requireSemver,","-          strictPreid: releaseGroup.releaseTag.strictPreid,","-        }","+      latestMatchingGitTag = await this.resolveLatestMatchingGitTag(","+        releaseGroup,","+        projectName,","+        preid","       );","-      this.cachedLatestMatchingGitTag.set(projectName, latestMatchingGitTag);","     }"," ","     return resolveCurrentVersion(","@@ -729,6 +719,45 @@ export class ReleaseGraph {","     );","   }"," ","+  /**","+   * Resolve and cache the latest git tag matching the release tag pattern of","+   * the given project's release group.","+   *","+   * @internal","+   */","+  async resolveLatestMatchingGitTag(","+    releaseGroup: ReleaseGroupWithName,","+    projectName: string,","+    preid: string","+  ): Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof getLatestGitTagForPattern>>> {","+    const latestMatchingGitTag = await getLatestGitTagForPattern(","+      releaseGroup.releaseTag.pattern,","+      {","+        projectName: sanitizeProjectNameForGitTag(projectName),","+        releaseGroupName: releaseGroup.name,","+      },","+      this.resolveRepositoryTags.bind(this),","+      {","+        checkAllBranchesWhen: releaseGroup.releaseTag.checkAllBranchesWhen,","+        preid: preid,","+        requireSemver: releaseGroup.releaseTag.requireSemver,","+        strictPreid: releaseGroup.releaseTag.strictPreid,","+      }","+    );","+    this.cachedLatestMatchingGitTag.set(projectName, latestMatchingGitTag);","+    return latestMatchingGitTag;","+  }","+","+  /**","+   * The projects matched by the user's filters, before any dependents were","+   * added according to `updateDependents`.","+   *","+   * @internal","+   */","+  getOriginallyFilteredProjects(): ReadonlySet<string> {","+    return this.originalFilteredProjects;","+  }","+","   /**","    * Resolve and cache the current version of a dependency that is not already","    * being versioned. Ecosystem-specific VersionActions call this lazily when"],"additions":43,"deletions":14,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/command-line/release/version.ts","lines":["@@ -44,6 +44,12 @@ import {"," } from './utils/shared';"," import { validateResolvedVersionPlansAgainstFilter } from './utils/version-plan-utils';"," import { ReleaseGroupProcessor } from './version/release-group-processor';","+import {","+  ReleaseBoundaryCheckError,","+  ReleaseBoundaryFinding,","+  checkReleaseBoundary,","+  formatReleaseBoundaryFinding,","+} from './version/release-boundary-check';"," import { SemverBumpType } from './version/version-actions';"," "," export interface NxReleaseVersionResult {","@@ -64,6 +70,10 @@ export interface NxReleaseVersionResult {","    * This can be passed to subsequent operations (changelog, publish) to avoid recomputing.","    */","   releaseGraph: ReleaseGraph;","+  /**","+   * Findings of the release boundary check. Only present when `release.version.releaseBoundaryCheck` is not \"off\".","+   */","+  releaseBoundaryFindings?: ReleaseBoundaryFinding[];"," }"," "," export const releaseVersionCLIHandler = (args: VersionOptions) =>","@@ -256,9 +266,36 @@ export function createAPI(","       }","     );"," ","+    const releaseBoundaryCheck =","+      nxReleaseConfig.version.releaseBoundaryCheck ?? 'off';","+    let releaseBoundaryFindings: ReleaseBoundaryFinding[] | undefined;","+","     try {","       await processor.processGroups();"," ","+      if (releaseBoundaryCheck !== 'off') {","+        releaseBoundaryFindings = await checkReleaseBoundary({","+          tree,","+          projectGraph,","+          nxReleaseConfig,","+          releaseGraph,","+          versionData: processor.getVersionData(),","+          preid: args.preid ?? '',","+          userGivenSpecifier: args.specifier,","+        });","+        if (releaseBoundaryFindings.length) {","+          if (releaseBoundaryCheck === 'error') {","+            throw new ReleaseBoundaryCheckError(releaseBoundaryFindings);","+          }","+          output.warn({","+            title: `The release boundary check found ${releaseBoundaryFindings.length} issue(s)`,","+            bodyLines: releaseBoundaryFindings.map(","+              (f) => `- ${formatReleaseBoundaryFinding(f)}`","+            ),","+          });","+        }","+      }","+","       // Delete processed version plan files if applicable","       if (args.deleteVersionPlans) {","         processor.deleteProcessedVersionPlanFiles();","@@ -395,6 +432,7 @@ export function createAPI(","         workspaceVersion,","         projectsVersionData: versionData,","         releaseGraph,","+        ...(releaseBoundaryFindings && { releaseBoundaryFindings }),","       };","     }"," ","@@ -454,6 +492,7 @@ export function createAPI(","       workspaceVersion,","       projectsVersionData: versionData,","       releaseGraph,","+      ...(releaseBoundaryFindings && { releaseBoundaryFindings }),","     };","   };"," }"],"additions":39,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/nx/src/command-line/release/version/release-boundary-check.spec.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,589 @@","+// Module-level mock container - initialized early so vi.mock factories can reference it","+const mocks = {","+  deriveSpecifierFromConventionalCommits: vi.fn(),","+  resolveVersionActionsForProject: vi.fn(),","+  resolveCurrentVersion: vi.fn(),","+  getLatestGitTagForPattern: vi.fn(),","+  readRawVersionPlans: vi.fn(),","+};","+","+vi.mock('./derive-specifier-from-conventional-commits', () => ({","+  deriveSpecifierFromConventionalCommits: (...args: any[]) =>","+    mocks.deriveSpecifierFromConventionalCommits(...args),","+}));","+","+vi.mock('./version-actions', async () => {","+  const actual = await vi.importActual('./version-actions');","+  return {","+    ...actual,","+    resolveVersionActionsForProject: (...args: any[]) =>","+      mocks.resolveVersionActionsForProject(...args),","+  };","+});","+","+vi.mock('./project-logger', async () => {","+  const actual = await vi.importActual('./project-logger');","+  return {","+    ...actual,","+    ProjectLogger: class ProjectLogger {","+      buffer() {}","+      flush() {}","+    },","+  };","+});","+","+vi.mock('./resolve-current-version', () => ({","+  resolveCurrentVersion: (...args: any[]) =>","+    mocks.resolveCurrentVersion(...args),","+}));","+","+vi.mock('../config/version-plans', async () => {","+  const actual = await vi.importActual('../config/version-plans');","+  return {","+    ...actual,","+    readRawVersionPlans: (...args: any[]) => mocks.readRawVersionPlans(...args),","+  };","+});","+","+vi.mock('../utils/git', async () => {","+  const actual = await vi.importActual('../utils/git');","+  return {","+    ...actual,","+    getLatestGitTagForPattern: (...args: any[]) =>","+      mocks.getLatestGitTagForPattern(...args),","+  };","+});","+","+import type { NxJsonConfiguration } from '../../../config/nx-json';","+import { createTreeWithEmptyWorkspace } from '../../../generators/testing-utils/create-tree-with-empty-workspace';","+import type { Tree } from '../../../generators/tree';","+import { createReleaseGraph } from '../utils/release-graph';","+import {","+  checkReleaseBoundary,","+  formatReleaseBoundaryFinding,","+  ReleaseBoundaryCheckError,","+} from './release-boundary-check';","+import { ReleaseGroupProcessor } from './release-group-processor';","+import { NOOP_VERSION_ACTIONS } from './version-actions';","+import {","+  createNxReleaseConfigAndPopulateWorkspace,","+  mockResolveVersionActionsForProjectImplementation,","+} from './test-utils';","+","+// A daemon connection would keep the test process alive after the run","+process.env.NX_DAEMON = 'false';","+","+describe('checkReleaseBoundary', () => {","+  let tree: Tree;","+","+  beforeEach(() => {","+    tree = createTreeWithEmptyWorkspace();","+    vi.resetAllMocks();","+    mocks.resolveVersionActionsForProject.mockImplementation(","+      mockResolveVersionActionsForProjectImplementation","+    );","+    mocks.getLatestGitTagForPattern.mockImplementation(","+      (_pattern, { projectName }) => ({","+        tag: `${projectName}@1.0.0`,","+        extractedVersion: '1.0.0',","+      })","+    );","+  });","+","+  async function runCheck(","+    graphDefinition: string,","+    releaseConfig: NxJsonConfiguration['release'],","+    filters: { projects?: string[]; groups?: string[] },","+    bumps: Record<string, string>,","+    {","+      userGivenSpecifier,","+      beforeCheck,","+    }: {","+      userGivenSpecifier?: string;","+      beforeCheck?: (","+        releaseGraph: Awaited<ReturnType<typeof createReleaseGraph>>","+      ) => void;","+    } = {}","+  ) {","+    mocks.deriveSpecifierFromConventionalCommits.mockImplementation(","+      (_, __, ___, ____, { name }) => bumps[name] ?? 'none'","+    );","+    const { nxReleaseConfig, projectGraph } =","+      await createNxReleaseConfigAndPopulateWorkspace(","+        tree,","+        graphDefinition,","+        releaseConfig,","+        mocks.resolveCurrentVersion,","+        filters","+      );","+    const releaseGraph = await createReleaseGraph({","+      tree,","+      projectGraph,","+      nxReleaseConfig,","+      filters,","+      firstRelease: false,","+      verbose: false,","+    });","+    const processor = new ReleaseGroupProcessor(","+      tree,","+      projectGraph,","+      nxReleaseConfig,","+      releaseGraph,","+      {","+        dryRun: false,","+        verbose: false,","+        firstRelease: false,","+        preid: '',","+        userGivenSpecifier: userGivenSpecifier as any,","+        filters,","+      }","+    );","+    await processor.processGroups();","+    beforeCheck?.(releaseGraph);","+    return checkReleaseBoundary({","+      tree,","+      projectGraph,","+      nxReleaseConfig,","+      releaseGraph,","+      versionData: processor.getVersionData(),","+      preid: '',","+      userGivenSpecifier,","+    });","+  }","+","+  const dependentInOtherGroup = `","+    groupA ({ \"projectsRelationship\": \"independent\" }):","+      - pkg-a@1.0.0 [js]","+        -> depends on ^pkg-c","+      - pkg-c@1.0.0 [js]","+    groupB ({ \"projectsRelationship\": \"independent\" }):","+      - pkg-b@1.0.0 [js]","+        -> depends on ^pkg-c","+  `;","+","+  it('should report a project from another group that updateDependents \"always\" added to the release', async () => {","+    const findings = await runCheck(","+      dependentInOtherGroup,","+      { version: { conventionalCommits: true } },","+      { groups: ['groupA'] },","+      { 'pkg-c': 'minor' }","+    );","+","+    expect(findings).toEqual([","+      {","+        type: 'added-by-dependents',","+        project: 'pkg-b',","+        releaseGroup: 'groupB',","+        newVersion: '1.0.1',","+        releasedDependencies: ['pkg-c'],","+      },","+    ]);","+  });","+","+  it('should report a dependent in another group whose range admits the new version when it is not released', async () => {","+    const findings = await runCheck(","+      dependentInOtherGroup,","+      { version: { conventionalCommits: true, updateDependents: 'auto' } },","+      { groups: ['groupA'] },","+      { 'pkg-c': 'minor' }","+    );","+","+    expect(findings).toEqual([","+      {","+        type: 'dependent-not-released',","+        project: 'pkg-b',","+        releaseGroup: 'groupB',","+        dependency: 'pkg-c',","+        dependencyNewVersion: '1.1.0',","+        declaredVersion: '^1.0.0',","+        dependencyCollection: 'dependencies',","+        declaredVersionAdmitsNewVersion: true,","+      },","+    ]);","+  });","+","+  it('should report a dependent whose exact version excludes the new version when it is not released', async () => {","+    const findings = await runCheck(","+      `","+        groupA ({ \"projectsRelationship\": \"independent\" }):","+          - pkg-a@1.0.0 [js]","+          - pkg-c@1.0.0 [js]","+        groupB ({ \